            <ArticleTitle>[Pilot study on knowledge about asthma and its treatment among Spanish teachers].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>452-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">This was a study aimed to know the knowledge about asthma.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SUBJECTS AND METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">933 teachers of 27 schools from 7 cities (children aged between 4 and 15 years) using a self-administered questionnaire Half of them knew asthma prevalence and its hereditary nature. Nearly all related asthma with allergy, 38% with exercise, 25%had students who suffered from asthma attacks in the school, and 91% admitted to have limited information and wish to improve it.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Our survey reveals that Spanish teachers have a limited information about asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
